assistant: Subject: parse numeric created_at from vendor 2026-10-01

I couldn't find the cause of the alert in shop-mcp's code, and this commit does not fix it. `create_order` passed the vendor's 200 response through correctly (o-5002, total 1499). The probe then sent the right request, `GET /orders/o-5002`, and the vendor answered 404. So on vendor API version 2026-10-01, an order the vendor confirmed could not be read back; the order should still be treated as unconfirmed. One guess is the `Idempotency-Key` header, which the spec lists as "recommended" for creating orders. Nothing in the evidence shows it matters, and adding it would break the v1 fixtures, because the test replay compares header names. This needs to go to the vendor, or be captured as a full v2 trace. What I did fix is a related v2 bug in the same trace. The new version sends `created_at` as a number (milliseconds since 1970) instead of an ISO date string. `get_order` read that as an invalid date and would have reported every v2 order as placed on 1970-01-01. It now handles numbers directly, and v1 ISO strings work as before. Typecheck, lint and tests pass, and the v1 fixtures give the same output, though no v2 fixture or trace exists to test the new path.

